1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,369
One prompt goes to one teacher.

2
00:00:02,369 --> 00:00:04,600
But the loss is averaged over tokens,

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,373
so whoever writes longer gets more of the say.

4
00:00:07,373 --> 00:00:10,388
Instruction following holds a fifth of the prompts

5
00:00:10,388 --> 00:00:12,860
and 1 to 3 percent of the trained tokens.

6
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:17,648
Multi-teacher on-policy distillation runs in three stages.

7
00:00:17,648 --> 00:00:21,209
General supervised fine-tuning gives one starting point.

8
00:00:21,209 --> 00:00:23,880
Each domain then trains its own RL expert,

9
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:27,568
one for math, one for code, one for instruction following.

10
00:00:27,568 --> 00:00:29,348
The fusion stage comes last,

11
00:00:29,348 --> 00:00:32,464
and there the student writes every answer itself.

12
00:00:33,564 --> 00:00:36,231
The teacher never writes a single token.

13
00:00:36,231 --> 00:00:38,164
It reads the student's answer

14
00:00:38,164 --> 00:00:41,164
and returns a distribution at every position.

15
00:00:41,164 --> 00:00:43,831
The student learns from its own writing,

16
00:00:43,831 --> 00:00:46,764
so an early mistake no longer moves it away.

17
00:00:47,864 --> 00:00:52,078
A public experiment ran sixty steps with three real experts,

18
00:00:52,078 --> 00:00:55,028
about one percent of the paper's training.

19
00:00:55,028 --> 00:00:57,275
Distance to math and code falls.

20
00:00:57,275 --> 00:01:00,435
Distance to instruction following stays flat.

21
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:03,104
The evaluation follows the same shape.

22
00:01:04,204 --> 00:01:07,913
The paper calls it token budget misallocation.

23
00:01:07,913 --> 00:01:10,170
Same student, same teachers,

24
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:14,846
the standard recipe recovers 35.6 percent of the headroom.

25
00:01:14,846 --> 00:01:17,668
With the three fixes, 83.4 percent.

26
00:01:18,768 --> 00:01:22,380
Inside T R L, three values change the accounting.

27
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:24,666
beta defaults to 0, forward KL,

28
00:01:24,666 --> 00:01:27,467
while stage three of the paper uses 1.

29
00:01:27,467 --> 00:01:30,564
top k only shapes anything when beta is 0.

30
00:01:30,564 --> 00:01:34,176
And every teacher shares the student's tokenizer.

31
00:01:35,276 --> 00:01:38,271
The fusion stage runs five processes at once.

32
00:01:38,271 --> 00:01:41,799
On four H 200s, one server generates for the student,

33
00:01:41,799 --> 00:01:44,262
two serve three teachers, one trains.

34
00:01:44,262 --> 00:01:45,926
The teachers stay frozen,

35
00:01:45,926 --> 00:01:48,788
and only the student's weights travel back.

36
00:01:49,888 --> 00:01:53,263
Open the training log and look at teacher token frac.

37
00:01:53,263 --> 00:01:56,637
A starved teacher still reports a healthy divergence.

38
00:01:56,637 --> 00:01:59,248
Only the token share tells you the truth.
